          "court": "Supreme Court of the United States",
          "year": 1972,
          "date_decided": "1972-04-03",
          "holding": "The Supreme Court reversed, holding that a State may not take children from an unwed father, presumed unfit by statute, without a hearing on his actual fitness as a parent.",
          "relevance": "Confirms that protective measures separating a parent from a child must rest on individualized findings.",
          "quote": "Under the Due Process Clause that advantage is insufficient to justify refusing a father a hearing when the issue at stake is the dismemberment of his family.",
